---
title: Hummus
servings: 6
tags: [middle eastern, vegan, quick]
cuisine: middle eastern
time: 5 minutes
source: Hummus by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/hummus/
---

Drain the @canned chickpeas{400%g}(1 can) into a bowl so you keep the liquid.
Set about ten chickpeas aside for the top.

Put the rest of the chickpeas in a #food processor{} with the
@garlic{1%clove}(minced), @lemon juice{1/4%cup},
@tahini{1/2%cup}(stirred well first) and @extra virgin olive oil{1/3%cup}.
Blend to a paste.

Add @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and a pinch of @black pepper{}, then pour in 1/4 cup
of the can liquid and blend ~{2%minutes}, until smooth.

Taste for lemon and salt. Loosen with more chickpea liquid until it drops
softly off a spoon.

Spread it in a shallow bowl, swirl with the back of a spoon, and top with the
saved chickpeas, more @extra virgin olive oil{} and a pinch of @paprika{}.

> For the smoothest hummus, rub the skins off the chickpeas in a bowl of water,
> or microwave them in their liquid for 3 minutes and blend while hot.

Serve at room temperature. It keeps five days in the fridge.
